# Creating and Saving a Text File in C#

This program uses `SaveFileDialog` to allow the user to choose where to save a text file. When the user clicks Save, `File.CreateText()` creates the file, and `WriteLine()` writes two names into it. The `Close()` method closes the file after writing. A message confirms whether the file was saved successfully or canceled.

