# Creating and Saving a Text File in C#

This program uses `SaveFileDialog` to let the user choose where to save a text file. If the user clicks OK, `File.CreateText()` creates the file, and `WriteLine()` writes three lines of text into it. The `Close()` method closes the file after writing, and `MessageBox.Show()` displays a success message. If the user cancels, the program does not save the file.

