# Reading a Text File in C#

This program uses `OpenFileDialog` to allow the user to select a text file to open. If the user clicks OK, `File.OpenText()` opens the selected file, and a `while` loop reads the file line by line using `ReadLine()`. Each line is displayed in `listBox1` using `Items.Add()`. If the user cancels the operation, `MessageBox.Show()` displays a message indicating that the file was not opened.
